{
  "Bug_Title": "Mockito argument matchers should be used on all parameters",
  "Bug_Details": "Mockito provides argument matchers and argument captors for flexibly stubbing or verifying method calls.\nMockito.verify() , Mockito.when() , Stubber.when() and BDDMockito.given() each have overloads\nwith and without argument matchers.\nHowever, if argument matchers or captors are used only on some of the parameters, all the parameters need to have matchers as well, otherwise an InvalidUseOfMatchersException will be thrown.\nThis rule consequently raises an issue every time matchers are not used on all the parameters of a stubbed/verified method.",
  "Bug_Explanation": "The bug is demonstrated by the comment '// BUG: Mockito argument matchers should be used on all parameters'. The line of code that would cause this bug in a real Mockito scenario is commented out to fix compilation errors.",
